    {
      "id": "7bcabe0f-0b0d-46dd-b5b8-e23b9966f2cc",
      "name": "Overview and setup",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        480,
        160
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 1,
        "width": 520,
        "height": 900,
        "content": "# Scrape Google Maps places to Google Sheets with Apify\n\n## Who's it for\n\nMarketers, founders, and anyone new to n8n who wants a shareable list of local places, such as cafes, restaurants, or co-working spaces, in a Google Sheet.\n\n## How it works\n\n- Reads the city, the search term, and the number of places from **Search settings**.\n- Creates a new Google Sheet named after your search.\n- Runs the Google Maps Scraper Actor on Apify and waits for the results.\n- Adds one row per place with name, rating, reviews, category, address, website, and Google Maps link.\n\n## How to set up\n\n1. Import the workflow into n8n.\n2. Open **Scrape Google Maps with Apify** and connect your Apify account. A free account is enough.\n3. Open **Create the spreadsheet** and sign in with Google. **Add places to the sheet** uses the same credential.\n4. Edit `city`, `query`, and `maxPlaces` in **Search settings**.\n5. Click **Execute workflow**, then open `spreadsheetUrl` in the output of **Create the spreadsheet**.\n\n## Requirements\n\n- An Apify account (the free plan works). Apify is the largest marketplace of tools for AI. 61,000 Actors to automate your business. This template uses the Google Maps Scraper Actor (`compass/crawler-google-places`).\n- A Google account with access to Google Sheets.\n\n## How to customize the workflow\n\nRaise `maxPlaces` for longer lists, add a Schedule Trigger to refresh the sheet every week, or swap in any other Actor from Apify Store."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
